     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "The base case of <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">n == 1</code> is not used in the function. When <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">n</code> is <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">0</code>, the overall multiplication becomes <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">0</code>. The recursion begins returning once the <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">n &lt; 0</code> base case is reached, initially returning <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">-1</code>. But the previous recursive call would return <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">0</code>, thereby zeroing out all computations and leaving an overall result of <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">0</code>."
